Required Checks Evidence
1. Request serialization limit
   Source: artifact_dagger.rs:16–21,251–278; artifact_dagger_process.rs:10–12,114–120.
   Expected: reject complete serialized requests >32768 bytes before consuming the attempt or invoking a runner; adapter and process launcher use one Rust MAX_REQUEST.
   Actual: shared bound and serialized-byte rejection precede Invocation consumption/dispatched.push/runner. New regression constructs valid phase JSON padded to exactly 16384 input bytes with escaped newlines, requires InvalidInput/no runner/no consumed attempt, then successfully dispatches a shorter input using the same attempt.
   Result: PASS, included in independent 50-test Rust run; exit 0.
2. Response serialization limit
   Source: protocol.py:8–10,127–143; main.py:26–48,127–142.
   Expected: complete JSON envelope <=65536 UTF-8 bytes, not merely a <=16384-byte body. Oversize raises typed Invalid and wrapper catches produce bounded prerequisite envelopes.
   Actual: response checks final encoded bytes. New regression covers control/backslash and Unicode/ASCII cases. Independent probes additionally confirmed exact 65536-byte envelope acceptance/round-trip, 65537 rejection as Invalid(response_size), bounded output or typed rejection for all non-NUL ASCII controls at 16384 body bytes, original-hash-bound fallback, and real size-check fallback through both pure and async fake-SDK Setup wrappers with an injected oversized encoded body. The injected body probes exercise error handling, not a claim that ordinary current Setup naturally produces such a body.
   Result: PASS; Python suite 67 passed, exit 0; supplemental probes exit 0.
3. Cancellation during independent verification
   Source: artifact_dagger_process.rs:228–275 and regression at 1483–1516.
   Expected: verifier sets cancellation then returns Verified: no successful Observation, no quiescent marker/pending removal; recreated runner with new identity remains fenced.
   Actual: full Budget check gates verifier entry and post-verifier eligibility; checks precede quiescent publication and pending removal; cancellation is checked before returning Observation. New deterministic fake verifier regression requires Interrupted, retained pending, absence of .quiescent, and OutcomeUnknown on recreated/new identity admission.
   Result: PASS, included in independent Rust suite. Cooperative cancellation checks are not an atomic cancellation/filesystem transaction or a hard-real-time syscall guarantee; neither is newly claimed.

